/home/yixunhu/codespace/xRIR_code/worklog/worklog_yixun/exp_06_oriented_cyl_claude/plan_oriented_cyl.md-112-- **H1b (channel effect)** — hallway C50, **C − F**: two-way 95 % upper bound < 0.
/home/yixunhu/codespace/xRIR_code/worklog/worklog_yixun/exp_06_oriented_cyl_claude/plan_oriented_cyl.md-113-- **H2 (descriptive screen, not a parity claim)** — all 11 room × metric cells for C − A: nominal and Bonferroni-adjusted two-way intervals (two-sided level 1 − 0.05/11, tails at 0.05/22 = 0.00227 and 0.99773, ≈ 114 draws per tail at `n_boot = 50 000`); cells with adjusted lower bound > 0 are reported as **detected harm**, cells with adjusted upper bound < 0 as **detected improvement**, all others as **no detected difference** — never as "non-inferior". The positive conclusion of the experiment rests on H1 together with H1b (see the overall reading).
